PPU re-anchoring of the upstream Relax SGLang patch.

Based on:
  PPU source   https://github.com/flytiger-eco/sglang-for-sail/tree/v0.5.17
               (sglang 0.5.17+v0.1.0.ppu2.2.0, as shipped in the base image)
  Relax patch  docker/patch/latest/sglang.patch
               (-> docker/patch/sglang/v0.5.17.patch), applied unchanged, with
               docker/patch/latest/sglang_per_pos_topk.patch after it

The upstream patch applies to that fork with seven hunks left unapplied; this
file places exactly those seven. Dockerfile.ppu asserts the two counts agree
before applying it, so a change on either side fails the build instead of
drifting silently.

Apply inside site-packages with -p2, between the two upstream patches:

  patch --batch --forward -p2 --fuzz=0 < sglang.patch
  patch --batch --forward -p2 --fuzz=0 < 0.5.17-ppu-adapt.patch
  patch --batch --forward -p2 --fuzz=0 < sglang_per_pos_topk.patch

Five hunks keep the upstream added and removed lines unchanged and differ only
in context or position:

  dsa_indexer.py  _maybe_repeat_query_heads   sits just before _get_q_k_bf16
  dsa_indexer.py  its second call site        PPU adds an `if self.use_fp4:` block after it
  memory_pool.py  memory_saver_adapter.region PPU adds an `if self.use_fp4_indexer:` block
  mxfp4.py        _pad_hopper_mxfp4_scale     PPU puts an `if is_ppu():` import block above it
  mxfp4.py        the weight-reload block     PPU renames the method body it wraps

Two carry what the fork's own code needs:

  kimi_k3.py      the _bfa_w merge call       PPU passes merge_mods / pad_rows instead of
                                              upstream's literal argument list
  kimi_k3.py      _k3_fused_decode_args       PPU also stacks the tuple into the buffer
                  reuse                       the decode kernel reads, so that one is
                                              kept captured too

